Security 6, JJWT, and PostgreSQL, deployed at zero cost on Render and Neon.

9
00:00:41,782 --> 00:00:45,122
Incoming HTTP requests pass through a

10
00:00:45,272 --> 00:00:49,169
strict Cross-Origin filter before reaching the JwtAuthenticationFilter.

11
00:00:49,319 --> 00:00:55,443
This component inspects the Authorization header for an HMAC-SHA256 Bearer token.

12
00:00:55,593 --> 00:00:59,490
Upon validating signature integrity and expiration, it

13
00:00:59,640 --> 00:01:04,093
sets the authentication principal in Spring Security's SecurityContextHolder.

14
00:01:04,243 --> 00:01:10,367
Downstream authorization gates enforce role-based access control, routing verified traffic through

15
00:01:10,517 --> 00:01:16,641
service and repository layers into a dedicated serverless Neon PostgreSQL database.

16
00:01:16,791 --> 00:01:20,131
In the interactive dashboard, a new

17
00:01:20,281 --> 00:01:24,178
