24
00:01:56,403 --> 00:02:03,083
Triggering verification unlocks the account and clears the token to prevent reuse.

25
00:02:03,233 --> 00:02:07,130
Next, we authenticate using our registered credentials.

26
00:02:07,280 --> 00:02:11,177
The backend queries PostgreSQL, returning a uniform

27
00:02:11,327 --> 00:02:15,781
InvalidCredentialsException if lookup fails, mitigating user enumeration attacks.

28
00:02:15,931 --> 00:02:21,498
Once BCrypt confirms the password hash and verifies activation, the

29
00:02:21,648 --> 00:02:27,215
JwtService generates a short-lived 15-minute access token signed with HMAC-SHA256.

30
00:02:27,365 --> 00:02:33,488
Simultaneously, a persistent 30-day UUID refresh token is saved to PostgreSQL.

31
00:02:33,638 --> 00:02:37,535
Inspecting the live claims, we see the

32
00:02:37,685 --> 00:02:42,139
